            <ArticleTitle>Renal auto-transplantation with interposed PTFE arterial graft: not necessarily a cure for loin pain/haematuria syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>134</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case report of a 23 year old man is described who was diagnosed with loin pain/haematuria syndrome. Despite auto-transplantation with interposed polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE)-prosthesis in the arterial anastomosis the symptoms recurred. A possible mechanism for the recurrent pain is proposed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
